    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hi i need help writing a rejection email. i'm a hiring manager and we just finished final interviews for a software engineer role but we decided to go with someone else. i want it to be polite and empathetic so they don't feel bad, but still professional. can you give me a template?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here is a template for your rejection email. It's important to be kind, even when you're saying no. You can start by thanking them for their time, which is a very polite gesture. Then, briefly state that you've moved forward with another candidate whose skills were a slightly closer match to the immediate needs of the role. Always end by wishing them the best in their job search.\n\n***\n\n**Subject: Update on the Software Engineer Position at [Company Name]**\n\nDear [Candidate Name],\n\nThank you so much for taking the time to interview with our team for the Software Engineer position. We truly enjoyed learning more about your background and experience during the final interviews. The caliber of candidates was very high, and we had a difficult decision to make.\n\nAfter careful consideration, we have decided to move forward with another candidate whose specific experience aligned most closely with the immediate needs of our team right now. This was a very tough choice, and we sincerely appreciate the effort you put into this process.\n\nWe were genuinely impressed with [mention something specific, e.g., your problem-solving approach or your enthusiasm for tech]. We wish you the very best of luck in your job search and future endeavors.",
